+// 0178: the depth mix's first product. K is the embedding width (2,304), M a block count
+// (1-8), N the query columns (1-8), and the tokens are a batch: both sides are activations,
+// and a token's slab steps by its own stride. The tiled GEMM serves it as a 64x64 tile per
+// 64 columns, so each work-group runs the whole 144-block K loop for a handful of outputs
+// (2.0 ms a call, 384 calls, 4.9 % of a prompt window, B60, profiled). Its own layout is the
+// split-K GEMV: one work-group a (token, column, row), the K split into 16-aligned slices,
+// the slices summed. GGML_OPENCL_F32_SMALL_M=1 turns it on; unset keeps today's selection.
